<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28944" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕtĭcŭlōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		metus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of fear</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Fearful, timid</i> (ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nullus est hoc meticulosus aeque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 1, 137</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 4, 2, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lepus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. p. 341, 9</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Frightful, terrible</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 5, 1, 52</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
